[37m* `solver="PGS"` — projected Gauss-Seidel converges for this tiny constraint set in ≤ 34 iterations (cost ~3 µs instead of 150 µs).[0m
[37m* `tolerance="1e-12"` — PGS is first-order; at the default 1e-8 it stops slightly short (final-state error ~1e-6). Tightening it makes the tuned model *more* converged than the reference's Newton tolerance, dropping the deviation to ~1e-8 at zero measurable cost.[0m
[37m* `iterations="100"` — generous cap (observed max 34, so runtime is never iteration-bound).[0m
[37m* `jacobian="dense"` — explicit; the auto-selected sparse path is actually slower here (nv=118), saving another ~9 µs/step.[0m

